SwiftPutty local patch 0014
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; should be (a password can be exposed)

Pre-connect command: blank the proxy credentials in the temporary copy
of the Conf, not in the session's own.

new_main_connection() copies the Conf to format the pre-connect command
and means to blank the proxy user name and password in the copy, so that
%user and %pass are reported as unsupported. It blanked them in the
session's Conf instead. So:

  - %pass in the command expanded to the proxy password, which was then
    visible in the process list and written to the Event Log ("Running
    pre-connect command: ...");
  - the session lost its proxy credentials, so a proxy needing them
    failed whenever a pre-connect command was set.

Found by code review for SwiftPutty M13; tested by
Core/tests/spb_backends_test.c.

--- a/proxy/newmain.c
+++ b/proxy/newmain.c
@@ -313,8 +313,8 @@
     assert(template);
     if (*template) {
         Conf *tmpconf = conf_copy(conf);
-        conf_set_str(conf, CONF_proxy_username, "");
-        conf_set_str(conf, CONF_proxy_password, "");
+        conf_set_str(tmpconf, CONF_proxy_username, "");
+        conf_set_str(tmpconf, CONF_proxy_password, "");
         unsigned flags;
         command = format_connection_setup_command(
             template, addr, port, tmpconf, &flags);
